{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/cc55a08f71cd75f0dda356149a61e9ab78536ecbb4644b88f840122863b92b88.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-96089/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0e7e0a0-9388-5346-ab96-f2dec237c9f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96089"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499/selection/58c972e79ddddb970abb4e9f7311810caf50e76f46ad4c4660ca30abf0878b2a" :answer/id #uuid "f9868f28-de0e-5239-8da3-af4d3175b86b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/8255d8370e49983ff0e37b5068a8a997de5eeadaedf7bd7869cf5dcd3c826ca1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499/selection/5dc5285e501f92504aedf271681286c93a46c824d78dec430e897ff999b33907" :answer/id #uuid "4cccb285-81ea-525d-8139-55f6f09740a7" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/5b77994fcd8b675c439a37e1b2049c0c6d266f12b3dc298b3183133b9010c818.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499/selection/862820f61639dabca6e8c4f621705526773e652cdc5530b276f9e5244e6bbd67" :answer/id #uuid "ba35b4c9-28e4-50f2-acc6-caa219327178" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/c4f19e6b424610387a8973b037c3f4636c09dba441ab1d6bd36dbe103d779a88.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499/selection/b608c45184e5f9ff1d81e450fda4c7d8c5cc261178ee0b4eb392e4b6edfd88e1" :answer/id #uuid "161738d1-4ee8-5b24-9717-d7acb367e108" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/770f3089576cabd68f3c80b597eb4f15df279538c49853526b0ea123bc75af08.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499/selection/d6efc5c33a57e45dd81a415ed3fcd72c1026062c6c42667942d2ade31f733663" :answer/id #uuid "b0e7ab6b-46dd-5f70-8278-f2c308e4e503" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e1ca6081e8077bcbc54de6a71e10ef1d278bbbc6b99842f1eee0d3dfcb71ebda.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3cd17a1-2a2a-52f2-91a6-65ee28d036f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80499/selection/d6efc5c33a57e45dd81a415ed3fcd72c1026062c6c42667942d2ade31f733663" :answer-field/choices ["q-80499/selection/58c972e79ddddb970abb4e9f7311810caf50e76f46ad4c4660ca30abf0878b2a" "q-80499/selection/5dc5285e501f92504aedf271681286c93a46c824d78dec430e897ff999b33907" "q-80499/selection/862820f61639dabca6e8c4f621705526773e652cdc5530b276f9e5244e6bbd67" "q-80499/selection/b608c45184e5f9ff1d81e450fda4c7d8c5cc261178ee0b4eb392e4b6edfd88e1" "q-80499/selection/d6efc5c33a57e45dd81a415ed3fcd72c1026062c6c42667942d2ade31f733663"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80499" :question/id #uuid "a02659d4-1cf7-5679-b691-6c43c4b6a900" :question/math-academy-id "q-80499" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+2y}{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(4,-2),(2,1),$ and $(-1,3).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(4,-2)}=\\frac{4+2(-2)}{4}=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,1)}=\\frac{2+2(1)}{4}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=\\frac{-1+2(3)}{4}=\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e1ca6081e8077bcbc54de6a71e10ef1d278bbbc6b99842f1eee0d3dfcb71ebda.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80499/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0e7e0a0-9388-5346-ab96-f2dec237c9f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80499"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6287a386-f422-5c2d-b40c-e1447f79bbdd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cf1d1082-7860-54a4-8bdd-a23e6d2a98e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a8b11a80-d54c-5c20-8ca1-0d5a85923fea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b89fe567-fefa-5be0-938e-fc3953ff41c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "8b83e57d-9a69-5959-b220-d0d8155684be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e44d7e6-fbc8-5549-aeaa-5839f4bffd01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119766/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-119766/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-119766/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-119766/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-119766/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-119766/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119766" :question/id #uuid "02428a19-79c0-54a0-bd59-933e59271090" :question/math-academy-id "q-119766" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=6xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=6xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119766/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119766"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "3c50c7a8-f19c-5603-abf0-0800c3ba5b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e86856bc-893c-51f6-b142-158d5018acb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "0cdaef1e-ecba-55ec-94b1-0af278746d83" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0aa231d0-b201-55b9-99d5-595cf3ae5262" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "9b003e80-650e-5a96-863c-187e130a982f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06c74166-797e-51e1-8ab6-8b9bfa7f2935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119769/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-119769/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-119769/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-119769/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-119769/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-119769/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119769" :question/id #uuid "686d59ed-d90f-5bf3-b657-f82ebc498b64" :question/math-academy-id "q-119769" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-5xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-5xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119769/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "3f9ac6b4-1eb7-5953-b69f-e0bab75c2bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "8db20139-ef29-523c-a82a-f9d854047d68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "499565f9-007d-5936-bd34-710fa288127a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "21c900e3-5727-5d2a-a848-ee7f02b4ccb7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "64dd550e-4a4a-518b-a8d6-c2fed808d822" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "98c30d2d-b036-5c2d-8a6e-4fbcd0750f04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97487/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-97487/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-97487/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-97487/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-97487/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-97487/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97487" :question/id #uuid "2bd68dbe-3df6-5a5a-89ed-3e22835c94e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-97487" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4x{y}^{2}$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-4x{y}^{2}.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/96c937cf10d45d8870a4a56e257d184dcf2e4caf11312c05df9f385f9c5ee7a8.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-97487/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97487"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "e2825df1-2696-5fa6-9073-c454074ad8d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "90663044-8663-5cc1-a6b9-27621fb7e245" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ec25e4e6-2778-52d3-94e0-cb4de63c8b17" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "a5e82298-1404-5124-852f-cdaed09f250d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c6be1802-65aa-564a-9b3a-099c23b2398b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f4099eba-f208-5df9-84e3-d9718331e137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97477/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-97477/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-97477/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-97477/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-97477/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-97477/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97477" :question/id #uuid "69d9aef9-325a-5644-bfec-8ec831c2020d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97477" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97477/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "118904e6-b7a6-5b56-a978-63740c93ec1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "fad19dfe-307a-5d61-8c24-9f539ccf710e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "21b8a7ee-f836-59dc-beba-66b8fb1adf1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6ca9ac4b-05ec-58f5-b491-cb21959da3e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "cc9e58d7-6d4c-5ab9-a11d-555e57ec8fb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eeebcd87-2d1b-5826-ba9a-116dbe1b768c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97482/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-97482/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-97482/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-97482/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-97482/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-97482/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97482" :question/id #uuid "d8725af0-96f6-534d-ac16-7589cb968544" :question/math-academy-id "q-97482" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=9xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=9xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97482/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97482"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "2d8b7c89-51ff-52b0-a9ae-f899df6b2cf2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "be16bd2c-17ad-559c-b6c8-11f54ab7412a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "97aeebcf-69eb-5843-8528-e1509c33e80f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "4bc7131d-24d1-5376-b9a9-b6429500c1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cfd6a72a-c6f5-5445-b37b-a262046aa130" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "baea9539-85ef-5cfd-aa31-a54f312f1da3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119797/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-119797/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-119797/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-119797/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-119797/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-119797/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119797" :question/id #uuid "3abc4afa-25ba-5703-a666-45b550ee045a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119797" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(2-x)(y+1)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(2-x)(y+1).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=2$ or $y=-1.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/caa61190f1a5565c58838556529715c08f9f00402c6f4b3ccb99a914e748f198.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/01e91ecf01cfc64ed87e29081a6b9f8a3fc5afade1b25be08039b8778d981cf7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $x>2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "de1ea38f-e71a-534b-9d98-d521afdb83d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0f4dcfe4-7ec8-5a3b-826f-fc466b7ad717" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c2d3f3bc-8b00-52e8-bb1c-440ea958e9d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "2fa97764-34fd-54c1-84ba-f4ced55fa470" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "accbf007-9725-5fc7-ba2c-f6686120129f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "022ab180-dbe3-585a-a6ec-ca5497bc5a3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119800/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer-field/choices ["q-119800/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-119800/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-119800/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-119800/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-119800/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119800" :question/id #uuid "7d5a91f8-7975-56de-b46e-33d895988c53" :question/math-academy-id "q-119800" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(1-x)(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y-2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=1$ or $y=2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/47784a3201e93648e495827b12078073cc9f1a03cd3c11904a875bad10a3bde2.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/73631c178777b4489e35fa87d08474ccf2b8b484b9bf5fe7272b1ce25d45f1b0.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<1$ and $y>2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x>1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $x<1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-119800/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119816/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "cff34d04-2bef-5503-83a8-9e00ad0e5fda" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119816/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b7ceeaa6-8909-50bd-8e0b-b66b881cfcc9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119816/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "320cc140-04b0-5fee-90bc-6f47239c594f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119816/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "609d26fc-8f06-5de3-832f-9b0a0729c0b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119816/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d2d8b810-ee16-55d2-9b9b-c421ab2ac297" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119816/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da5d8795