11747a3eb17e22333901bfb8fd3.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $x<2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $x<2$ and $y<-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>2$ and $y>-1,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-119816/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119816"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-97538"] :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+1)^{2}(y-2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1$ and $y>2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-1$ and $y<2,$ the slope of the slope field is negative" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x+1)^{2}(y-2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=-1$ or $y=2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/1f4b1b2ca736fb83eff0a4b85a3f479bf99b3b337492d0a77abe739038ed141f.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/fdafadd1631a75c2998aaed5c6bad62a3ea1dcc0ac57d245a00d167e74aa3bb4.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $x<-1$ and $y>2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $x<-1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x>-1$ and $y<2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b04163d6-827b-59c5-a05e-d100ca89fa6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "b7265f38-606f-596e-9c26-128f305fcd84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "770864f4-c3d3-5d88-96b5-131ce1bec3a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8b65d57c-7041-5c39-86b4-11038518e3c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c094514f-64b7-5499-9fb1-c2f85d3a561a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bdd2a90-88c4-544c-b468-eb943fd08ab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97495/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-97495/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-97495/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-97495/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-97495/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-97495/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97495" :question/id #uuid "4235049c-7cc2-5176-8c56-91624ea6b2f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97495" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(x+2)(y+2)$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x>-2$ and $y>-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-2$ and $y>-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive\n- At every point $(x,y)$ where $x<-2$ and $y<-2,$ the slope of the slope field is positive" :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=(x+2)(y+2).$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=-2$ or $y=-2.$ This divides the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/7d225d82eee3043380eda76506b28e81aee06d42a232348b91b0d5ceb04f3318.png)\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each of those four regions (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/bd9eedd3b8d82415e8f3126236f2e3a3b4e326a7072057bbd21406da92a08139.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. If $x>-2$ and $y>-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement II is false. If $x<-2$ and $y>-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in this region.\n\n- Statement III is true. If $x<-2$ and $y<-2,$ then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in this region." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97495/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75710e99-e13c-54ba-9401-486bfec15284"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97495"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233/selection/7a4264dc32e73943f716b740f169352f0b3eb0a5cd247ceeba9c451eef4870d6" :answer/id #uuid "b68b8662-70a5-5529-b3e2-cc51c6f2affb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/4e286da41a3a0026ff7ee55649be2f0bdf5209e407a0f6fe96b3bbffa1295fb5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233/selection/e8534b091d72ae3e2f17452a7c215085232629864bb6621fb78da7e3e8f7669f" :answer/id #uuid "a320db02-ff43-593a-965b-d0abeb3ae2f6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/0be25701c9d678977655081af50779401b207cbcd91a4c04cb32e8740180ae45.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233/selection/730cf1b98e88d81599ed72300307a81e3e9ba8a76ba066234adb4499a28fca33" :answer/id #uuid "4438b094-9cee-5477-b04c-9ec37ed9b311" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ae2c8de966219eb473c42fa809bfde49b52c7c88efaf83fc7ab0d602d734e722.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233/selection/d33cbd1a55ae08df0f80249c8d0c8148ba62443bd259a7d6ad2b8a3ac79aeb7c" :answer/id #uuid "9c8c07c2-15e3-5a2c-a800-406a8c65d4e5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/b433458640a60ab79880fe94549be1071420948c1c809d5c43576d4aeed45510.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233/selection/7d632e120fc98ab710224b9a7e1eb38d34b473cc15e275d341a150838c13d8df" :answer/id #uuid "9d5a4483-d21e-50c9-87e3-eb3faa0fb89d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/8b5ff8f702e76cb7108ae458447b38eed4d18e38336f54279f25d1c59c02e3b4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f5e91d6-7b03-535a-9b7c-caad50ff324a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98233/selection/730cf1b98e88d81599ed72300307a81e3e9ba8a76ba066234adb4499a28fca33" :answer-field/choices ["q-98233/selection/7a4264dc32e73943f716b740f169352f0b3eb0a5cd247ceeba9c451eef4870d6" "q-98233/selection/e8534b091d72ae3e2f17452a7c215085232629864bb6621fb78da7e3e8f7669f" "q-98233/selection/730cf1b98e88d81599ed72300307a81e3e9ba8a76ba066234adb4499a28fca33" "q-98233/selection/d33cbd1a55ae08df0f80249c8d0c8148ba62443bd259a7d6ad2b8a3ac79aeb7c" "q-98233/selection/7d632e120fc98ab710224b9a7e1eb38d34b473cc15e275d341a150838c13d8df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98233" :question/id #uuid "69047027-7fd9-581d-a6dd-06bc079f6f80" :question/math-academy-id "q-98233" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)$ varies with both $x$ and $y,$ which of the following **cannot** be the slope field for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we are given an equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is a function of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the slope field varies with both $x$ and $y.$\n\nOf the given slope fields, we note the following slope field does not vary with $x$ given a fixed value of $y.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/ae2c8de966219eb473c42fa809bfde49b52c7c88efaf83fc7ab0d602d734e722.png)\n\n \n\nTo see this more clearly, notice that if we draw a horizontal line, the slopes do not vary.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/e243f3fb7515d9858599775ce0391f85f1de237f08380e1ec3b7403b1ecdbf53.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-98233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2334101-5266-5853-aedf-04c85746b5cc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-119372/selection/66c71f73fa84c38bc527c883a79c768146b97498564d9958263a6ee80a7421bd" :answer/id #uuid "a741ce2d-0c24-5543-94a4-a1916c9d899f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/81bdcfd873677151067b3e2d542315d2f10f9b65f19a05ad3759dc5fe69a3704.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119372/selection/736043486f398ebd56ea0d788e023b76ad334f6792d03896a9a8785857a09730" :answer/id #uuid "92cc768d-ade3-5d5b-a862-3ac75591a7e6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/128c02e4d847e918cce92b38f4a7f09ffab6a11bf6f25ee7fd3480d6a6c3cac6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119372/selection/da13113ecaec3bd97c568fca7e42181c2bd2af7c8ac515ea64b6bd9aef32f2e8" :answer/id #uuid "3dbf2c4f-fe91-5a63-9fd7-a1913710d40b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/c74a4cf84ce908132b57674ef5624e0afcd42af7c40150ac0079e25894a60ba3.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119372/selection/506bf26c142b04696bb1d4af767a7f6d2eb01af6d82e4232d5c796674504bab8" :answer/id #uuid "55f2291f-cdd1-56ea-9c48-f0c5a1aa63a2" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/1fbb7d5a4a957b130c0835b09a6dba5c527e3b61844769b78f5517f4e4914b39.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119372/selection/004e0e2776a09bcd4160e80f9f6fe108a7e1716be5761957d848031f2c62b40b" :answer/id #uuid "f08a3d9b-88f8-574e-92ca-82bc6d6948c5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044888/assets/7d5df9fe81ebd1e656eefc97380ae646a1a4f64de51e4745bc31d822e022d65d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119372/selection" :answer-field/id